# R / RStudio state
.Rproj.user
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata

# Quarto cache / freeze
/.quarto/
/_freeze/
*_cache/
*_files/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Data files stay local; populate-data.sh is tracked so a new machine can re-fetch.
# Published data files are un-ignored by name below.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/README.md
# Published (2026-08-12), with a source credit on the Data page. ITT is openly
# distributed; its covariates are WDI + Polity, both open.
!data/ITT.csv
# Published (2026-08-19), linked from the Data page. CES common content is openly
# distributed via Harvard Dataverse. 13 MB, the largest tracked file here.
!data/ces.csv

# Reading PDFs — copyrighted, kept local. Citations are in refs606.bib.
readings/*
!readings/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Publishing is opt-in. Ignore sources and rendered output wholesale, then
# re-include each published page by name in the blocks below.
# To publish a page: add `!docs/<name>.html` (and `!<name>.qmd` if the source
# should be public too), render, run ./prune-search-index.sh, link it, commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Sources: ignore every .qmd, then re-include only the published pages.
*.qmd
!index.qmd
!about.qmd
!slides.qmd
!code.qmd
!mlesyllabus26.qmd
# released deck: linear model prediction methods
!predictionOLS26.qmd
# released deck: binary response models
!binarymodels26.qmd
# released deck: likelihood theory & estimation mechanics
!likelihood26.qmd
# released deck: maximizing the log-likelihood
!llfmax26.qmd
# released: codebook for the CES data used in exercise #1
!cescodebook26.qmd

# Rendered output: ignore everything under docs/, then re-include the published
# pages and the shared assets GitHub Pages needs to serve them.
docs/*
!docs/index.html
!docs/about.html
!docs/slides.html
!docs/code.html
!docs/mlesyllabus26.html
!docs/mlesyllabus26.pdf
# released deck: linear model prediction methods
!docs/predictionOLS26.html
# released deck: binary response models
!docs/binarymodels26.html
# released deck: likelihood theory & estimation mechanics
!docs/likelihood26.html
# released deck: maximizing the log-likelihood
!docs/llfmax26.html
# released: codebook for the CES data used in exercise #1
!docs/cescodebook26.html
# released EXERCISE: only the rendered page. `ex12026.qmd` stays ignored above --
# its figure chunks are the answers to questions 1-4.
!docs/ex12026.html
# released EXERCISE: only the rendered page. `ex22026.qmd` stays ignored above, and
# `ex22026answers.qmd`/`docs/ex22026answers.html` stay ignored permanently.
!docs/ex22026.html
# released ANSWER KEY, after exercise #1 was submitted. Only the rendered page --
# `ex12026answers.qmd` stays ignored above. Release a key only once the exercise
# it answers is in; `docs/ex22026answers.html` is NOT released (ex #2 is due
# 2026-09-02).
!docs/ex12026answers.html
!docs/styles.css
# Built from every page rendered into docs/, so it needs trimming to match the
# published set. Run ./prune-search-index.sh after each render, before committing.
!docs/search.json
!docs/site_libs/
# ...but NOT these generated libs: pages embed their own resources
# (embed-resources: true), so these are render byproducts, not site assets.
docs/site_libs/kePrint/
docs/site_libs/lightable/
docs/site_libs/revealjs/
# Same story for the htmlwidgets/plotly stack pulled in by interactive figures
# (versioned dir names, so match by prefix).
docs/site_libs/crosstalk*/
docs/site_libs/htmltools-fill*/
docs/site_libs/htmlwidgets*/
docs/site_libs/jquery*/
docs/site_libs/plotly-*/
docs/site_libs/typedarray*/
!docs/.nojekyll

# Side projects — not part of the course site.
flock-mle-assignment/
flock-placement/

# Loose scratch / deck assets at the repo root
Rplots.pdf
sandbox26.R
snoop.jpeg
zorntweet.png

# Companion .R scripts that ARE the answer to exercise #2 (hand-rolled Newton-
# Raphson for the logit: log-likelihood, score, Hessian, the loop, the SEs).
# Unlike binarymodels26.R these must never be published -- a single `git add -A`
# would put the graded work in the public repo as a plain script.
llfmax26.R
nr-logit.R
compare-hand-glm.R
maximization26.R

# PLSC 501 materials parked here — they belong to the 501 course, not this site.
Coding Challenges Sp 2026.pptx
challenge*-wage1-key.R

# Claude Code local project config
.claude/

# Project worklog — local only.
worklog.md

# Reference copies of superseded long-form decks (see _reference/README.md).
# Quarto ignores the directory; git should too -- the .html files are multi-MB
# self-contained renders and the .qmd sources follow the same "ignore sources"
# rule as every other topic deck above.
_reference/
